<title>JAPAN: Ajinomoto to merge three frozen food subsidiaries.</title>
<headline>Ajinomoto to merge three frozen food subsidiaries.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Japanese seasoning maker Ajinomoto Co Inc said on Tuesday it plans to merge three of its frozen food subsidiaries next April.</p>
<p>Ajinomoto will merge three regional subsidiaries in the hope of rationalising resources and strengthening its frozen food business, a spokesman for the company said.</p>
<p>The new firm is expected to be capitalised at 1.2 billion yen and will aim for annual sales of 140 billion to 150 billion yen, the spokesman said.</p>
</text>
